Package: ROpenEigen
Type: Package
Title: R Bindings for Eigen 5
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Qing", "Zhu", email = "20170458@alu.cqu.edu.cn",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: R interface to Eigen 5.  Dense matrices are exposed as
    reference objects that live on the C++ side, so a decomposition is
    computed once and reused rather than refactorised on every call.  Base R
    idioms -- matrix multiplication, solve(), determinant(), t(), the
    arithmetic and math groups and subscripting -- dispatch on those objects
    directly; the operations that are not generics in base R, such as det(),
    norm(), diag() and trace(), have 'eigen_'-prefixed equivalents.  The
    Eigen decompositions (Cholesky, LU, QR, SVD, eigenvalue) are available
    both as objects with methods and as one-shot functions.  Real sparse
    matrices are supported too, with sparse LU, Cholesky, QR, conjugate
    gradient, BiCGSTAB, GMRES, MINRES, DGMRES, IDRS and least-squares
    solvers that never densify the matrix.  Rotations, axis-angle vectors,
    quaternions and affine transforms from the Geometry module are wrapped
    as reference objects, and the SpecialFunctions and MatrixFunctions
    modules are exposed through 'eigen_'-prefixed elementwise and matrix
    functions.
